res\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"903b2ffa0d90fa2d80ace8ab087493f0003dcd1cb7f7b483e8b7a6462cc59a96","event_uuid":"0345f50c-ab91-4267-89d7-e4792402f0ee","position":{"commit_sha":"2aa76397b4449ec8f945bd180f0de6821d959808","position":"1785599851329470001-0345f50c-ab91-4267-89d7-e4792402f0ee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785372534995292001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"Set `merge.ours.driver=true` in the reconciler workflow so the tickets branch's\n`.bridge_state/* merge=ours` attribute actually resolves on GHA. Latent bug today; hard prerequisite\nfor B1. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why\n`init.py:508-511` sets `merge.ours.driver` **per clone**, and it is never committed;\n`reconcile-bridge.yml` never sets it. So on the runner the `merge=ours` attribute names an\n**undefined driver** and git silently falls back to a 3-way text merge of an **18,231,660-byte** JSON\nfile — the opposite of the local-wins behaviour the design assumes.\n\n**Scope correction (plan-review G6 remediation): the canary is NOT in scope.**\n`reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` does a bare `git worktree add` at `:88` but then calls **`rebar init`\nat `:146`**, and its own comment at `:138-140` explains why (\"a bare `git worktree add` of the\ntickets branch does NOT create ... and the write seam refuses every rebar write without it\"). So the\ncanary already gets `merge.ours.driver` via `_merge_ours_unit`. `reconcile-bridge.yml` does the bare\nworktree add at `:117` and **never** calls `rebar init`, which is why only it is affected. An earlier\ndraft listed both workflows; that was wrong.\n\nThis must land before B1: `blob:none` keeps commits but removes merge-base **blobs**, which the\nreconverge path materializes, so filtering while the driver is undefined makes an already-fragile\npath lazily fault large blobs mid-merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `reconcile-bridge.yml` sets `merge.ours.driver=true` for the tickets worktree before any merge\n      step. Tier: **unit** workflow-lint assertion.\n      Proving command: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py -v`.\n- [ ] The canary is asserted to obtain the driver via its existing `rebar init` call, so it needs no\n      edit — a regression guard against re-adding the change there. Tier: **unit** workflow-lint.\n- [ ] A reconverge against a **diverged** remote in a fresh runner-shaped checkout resolves\n      `.bridge_state/*` **local-wins** (not a text merge) and produces no conflict markers. Tier:\n      **integration** in a real temporary git repo mimicking the runner setup.\n- [ ] The same scenario **without** the config produces the text-merge behaviour — the negative\n      control proving the test detects the defect. Tier: **integration**.\n\n## Files\n`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, tests (the canary is deliberately untouched)\n\nScope: XS-S. No dependencies.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"set merge.ours.driver"},{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml","reason":"set merge.ours.driver"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","42eb-5789-c798-4dfc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"42eb-5789-c798-4dfc","parent_status_uuid":"9a9cae7c-335e-43bc-b2e3-43170c250e7d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"040e-3f0c-ae86-4212","ticket_type":"story","title":"B3: define merge.ours.driver on the reconciler runner (prerequisite for the CI clone filter)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2472890c-0421-4f0e-9dea-dcee403ee65d","852d7dc2-4a0f-4466-bf7c-28d4877a87aa","98b02206-4c2f-4a36-92b7-dc96e0c807b4","9fa4c3e3-fbb0-458a-9517-ada4b27826ca","378a0a53-4842-4cac-9b0a-488fc9a41c36","211b38d0-2b7c-4858-95aa-40599d2e421a","d9946a31-8fa6-42f6-8a28-35c7abcbf0f7","9a9cae7c-335e-43bc-b2e3-43170c250e7d","0345f50c-ab91-4267-89d7-e4792402f0ee"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785599851329470002,"uuid":"88ec5e6d-09c0-4ac1-98a8-19212467415c"}